## 1. Geometric Anti-Aliasing [CYD-AA-GEOM]

### 1.1 Current State [CYD-AA-GEOM-CURRENT]

> **STATUS 2026-08-14 — §1 IS BUILT.** The paragraph below describes the state *before*
> the AA work and is retained as the problem statement; it is no longer a description of
> the code. Verified at commit `153b050`: `fill_circle()` is the scanline rasterizer §1.4
> asked for, computing exact floating-point x-intercepts per row and applying
> `cov = 0.5 - dist` coverage to the edge pixels (`canvas_esp32.cpp:1027`, formula at
> `:1086`); `fill_rect()` precomputes per-side fractional edge coverage (`:673`, values at
> `:690-694`); `fill_round_rect()` applies fractional corner coverage (`:793`, at `:812`);
> `stamp_stroke_disc()` (`:1555`) is the round-cap stroking primitive, and
> `stroke_round_rect()` (`:934`), `stroke_rect()` (`:762`) and `stroke_circle()` (`:1172`)
> all reach AA through it — `stroke_circle` is a one-line delegation to `stroke_arc`
> (`:1174`), and `stroke_round_rect` draws its four corners with `stroke_arc` and its four
> straight edges with `fill_rect` strips (`:956-959`), so no primitive carries its own
> duplicate rasterizer. `fill_arc()` AA's the circular rim (`:1186`, coverage at `:1219`)
> and documents its two straight sector edges as a known hard-edged AA delta versus Skia
> (`:1177-1184`). `draw_line()` (`:1417`) **exceeds** §1.3, which asked
> only for perpendicular distance: thin strokes (`sw <= 1.5`) take a Xiaolin Wu path
> (`:1437-1446`) and wide strokes take a coverage-parallelogram path (`:1502`). §1.2's SDF
> formula is the one implemented, unchanged. No edit was needed to §1.2-§1.4.

`canvas_esp32.cpp` uses integer rasterization for all geometric primitives. `canvas_esp32.cpp:put_pixel` already implements full 8-bit alpha blending. The font atlas already provides 8-bit antialiased glyphs. Text rendering already blends glyph alpha with fill alpha. The gap is exclusively in geometric edge rendering.

### 1.2 Coverage-Based AA Approach [CYD-AA-GEOM-APPROACH]

For each geometric primitive, edge pixels compute a coverage value (0.0-1.0) representing what fraction of the pixel area the shape covers. This coverage multiplies the fill/stroke alpha and passes through the existing `put_pixel()` blend path.

**Signed distance field (SDF) method**: For each edge pixel, compute the signed distance from pixel center to the geometric boundary. Map distance to coverage:

```
coverage = clamp(0.5 - distance, 0.0, 1.0)
```

Where `distance` is in pixel units, negative = inside shape, positive = outside. This produces a 1-pixel-wide anti-aliased edge.

### 1.3 Primitives Requiring AA [CYD-AA-GEOM-PRIMITIVES]

| Primitive | Function | SDF Calculation |
|-----------|----------|-----------------|
| Filled circle | `fill_circle()` | `distance = sqrt((px-cx)^2 + (py-cy)^2) - radius` |
| Stroked circle | `stroke_circle()` | `distance = abs(sqrt((px-cx)^2 + (py-cy)^2) - radius) - half_thickness` |
| Filled rect | `fill_rect()` | Edge coverage at 4 borders (1D distance) |
| Stroked rect | `stroke_rect()` | Edge coverage at inner and outer boundaries |
| Stroke disc stamp | `stamp_stroke_disc()` | Same as filled circle — this is the round-cap stroking primitive used by `stroke_arc()` |
| Lines | `draw_line()` | Perpendicular distance from pixel center to line segment |

### 1.4 Implementation Notes [CYD-AA-GEOM-IMPL]

- Use integer-approximated SDF where possible. The `sqrt()` in circle SDF can use the existing integer distance comparison (`dx*dx + dy*dy` vs `r*r`) with a 1-pixel band around the boundary for AA computation. Only edge pixels pay the `sqrt()` cost.
- `fill_circle()` currently uses the midpoint circle algorithm. Replace with a scanline rasterizer that, for each row, computes the exact floating-point x-intercepts of the circle edge and applies coverage to the first and last pixel of each scanline.
- `stamp_stroke_disc()` is called many times per arc stroke. Performance matters here. Consider: precompute the disc coverage as a small lookup once per radius, then stamp from the lookup.
- Band rendering compatibility: all AA changes operate within the existing `in_band()` / `put_pixel()` pipeline. No architectural changes to band rendering.
- Color format: RGB565. Alpha blending happens at 8-bit precision in `put_pixel()`, then quantizes to 565 on write. This is already correct for AA — the blended result just gets quantized.

### 1.5 Compliance [CYD-AA-GEOM-COMPLIANCE]

### [CYD-AA-C1] Filled circles render with anti-aliased edges (no stairstepping visible at 240x320)
### [CYD-AA-C2] Stroked arcs render with anti-aliased edges via `stamp_stroke_disc()` AA
### [CYD-AA-C3] Filled and stroked rectangles render with anti-aliased edges
### [CYD-AA-C4] No increase in band buffer size (still 16 scanlines, 7,680 bytes)
### [CYD-AA-C5] Dashboard demo remains visually functional — no regression in layout or color

> **NOTE 2026-08-14 — C4's parenthetical is now build-dependent.** The AA work did not
> enlarge the band buffer and C4 is SATISFIED, but "16 scanlines" is no longer a universal
> constant: `kBandHeight` is `CXC_BAND_HEIGHT`, which defaults to 16
> (`src/canvas_esp32.h:35-38`, giving 240x16x2 = 7,680 bytes on the classic CYD) and is
> raised to a full frame with `-DCXC_BAND_HEIGHT=320` on the PSRAM-bearing build env
> (`src/CMakeLists.txt:331`). Read C4 as "AA introduced no per-band memory growth", which
> is what it was measuring. The rest of §1 is verified CURRENT as of this date — see the
> note at §1.1.

